{"version":3,"term":{"cols":80,"rows":24},"timestamp":1792777573,"command":"env ROOT=/var/tmp/ev508-tree/root-13-system-cycle-no-args /var/tmp/ev508-bin/emerge -p --depclean","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/bash"}}
[0.004, "o", "\u001b]0;portuale: emerge\u0007"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mAlways study the list of packages to be cleaned for any obvious\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mmistakes. Packages that are part of the world set will always\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mbe kept.  They can be manually added to this set with\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[32;01m`emerge --noreplace <atom>`\u001b[39;49;00m.  Packages that are listed in\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mpackage.provided (see portage(5)) will be removed by\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mdepclean, even if they are part of the world set.\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00m\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mAs a safety measure, depclean will not remove any packages\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00munless *all* required dependencies have been resolved.  As a\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mconsequence of this, it often becomes necessary to run \r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[32;01m`emerge --update --newuse --deep @world`\u001b[39;49;00m prior to depclean.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", ">>> No packages selected for removal by depclean\r\n>>> To see reverse dependencies, use --verbose\r\nPackages installed:   3\r\nPackages in world:    1\r\nPackages in system:   2\r\nRequired packages:    3\r\nNumber to remove:     0\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b]0;vivo@:/var/tmp/ev508-tree\u0007"]
